    "algorithm":  [
                      "Capture both supplied inputs without invoking caller-owned accessors or inherited iterators.",
                      "Strictly validate the canonical FOOD-007E capacity-source selection request.",
                      "Validate the reservation request and fulfillment intent through the canonical structural contracts required by FOOD-007E.",
                      "Require the reservation request fulfillment-intent reference and quote reference to agree with the canonical supplied fulfillment intent exactly as required by the FOOD-007M precedent.",
                      "Strictly validate canonical FOOD-007S governing-scope recorded-capacity arithmetic.",
                      "Require FOOD-007E SKU selections, request capacity requirements and FOOD-007S SKU arithmetic to have equal lengths and identical per-index SKU id/version.",
                      "Require each FOOD-007E selected SKU revision to equal the corresponding FOOD-007S governingRevision.",
                      "Reject reordered, missing, extra, duplicate or inconsistent SKU streams rather than sorting or repairing them.",
                      "Require the FOOD-007E selected fulfillment slot and FOOD-007S slot arithmetic to align exactly by method, locationReference, windowReference and selected revision/governingRevision.",
                      "Recheck each supplied FOOD-007S recorded arithmetic identity: recordedCapacityDelta must equal capacityUnits minus recordedHeldQuantity.",
                      "For every SKU, validate canonical positive-safe reservation demand quantity and compute recordedDemandAdjustedCapacityDelta = recordedCapacityDelta - demandQuantity.",
                      "For the selected fulfillment slot, use the canonical one-slot reservation demand quantity of 1 and compute recordedDemandAdjustedCapacityDelta = recordedCapacityDelta - 1.",
                      "Use BigInt subtraction for demand adjustment and reject a result outside the signed JavaScript safe-integer range.",
                      "Preserve positive, zero and negative arithmetic exactly; never clamp.",
                      "Return a detached and deeply frozen result."
